{"affected_record_refs":[],"blindness":{"answer_key_hidden":true,"benchmark_grade_hidden":true,"detector_identity_hidden":true,"exceptions":[],"other_reviews_hidden":true,"sc_referee_output_hidden":true},"bounded_statement":null,"case_id":"case:e4ba0f6377e3f52de641","completed_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:56.688906Z","confidence_used_for_labeling":false,"counterevidence_considered":[{"description":"The clip operation could in principle alter the exposure away from the authorized quantity; however, because predict_proba rows sum to 1 with nonnegative entries, the weighted expectation is mathematically bounded in [0, 2], leaving the values unchanged and fully continuous rather than confined to the finite level set.","evidence_id":"evidence:f4234fb7b8d8f5730900","record_refs":[],"source_refs":[{"content_digest":"sha256:daa2dd0f40c50bcdfb89818d0edc0f5eb098a67cc4b2425a022efae9d1d18d16","end_line":16,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L16-L16","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"shares = sorter.predict_proba(features)","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":16},{"content_digest":"sha256:daa2dd0f40c50bcdfb89818d0edc0f5eb098a67cc4b2425a022efae9d1d18d16","end_line":23,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L23-L23","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"bounded = np.clip(mean, 0.0, 2.0)","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":23}],"support_role":"counterevidence"}],"evidence":[{"description":"The exposure used is `bounded`, which is the continuous shares-weighted expected level index passed through np.clip on [0, 2]; since the expectation is a convex combination of {0, 1, 2}, it always lies within [0, 2] and the clip is an identity, so the exposure equals the authorized continuous quantity.","evidence_id":"evidence:17d3835a913f977b1d97","record_refs":[],"source_refs":[{"content_digest":"sha256:daa2dd0f40c50bcdfb89818d0edc0f5eb098a67cc4b2425a022efae9d1d18d16","end_line":18,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L18-L18","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"mean = shares @ np.array([0.0, 1.0, 2.0])","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":18},{"content_digest":"sha256:daa2dd0f40c50bcdfb89818d0edc0f5eb098a67cc4b2425a022efae9d1d18d16","end_line":23,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L23-L23","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"bounded = np.clip(mean, 0.0, 2.0)","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":23},{"content_digest":"sha256:daa2dd0f40c50bcdfb89818d0edc0f5eb098a67cc4b2425a022efae9d1d18d16","end_line":25,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L25-L25","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"exposure = bounded","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":25}],"support_role":"supports"},{"description":"The discrete level assignment is computed but never supplies the exposure position.","evidence_id":"evidence:44e29964bd0a0cb68837","record_refs":[],"source_refs":[{"content_digest":"sha256:daa2dd0f40c50bcdfb89818d0edc0f5eb098a67cc4b2425a022efae9d1d18d16","end_line":17,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L17-L17","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"label = sorter.predict(features)","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":17}],"support_role":"supports"}],"extensions":{"x-cross-case-evidence-used":false,"x-review-packet-digest":"sha256:504ce7cff73a0d08dc2800a82be5d6ee10328003bf9201b5f48ae2293e206b55","x-stage1-falsification-attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by asking whether clipping could collapse the exposure onto finite level values or whether `bounded` could differ from the authorized expectation: clipping to [0, 2] cannot map interior continuous values onto the set {0, 1, 2}, and since every row of predict_proba is a probability vector, mean is provably within [0, 2] and the clip is a no-op, so the exposure is exactly the authorized continuous expectation. No path from the discrete `label` to `exposure` exists. The attempt to establish the issue failed."},"issue_class":null,"provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"software:sc-referee-